{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v206l-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:55c86b94d333403e55b5", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly defines the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, not the complete planned set.", "observed_value": "target = retained post-screening subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result is explicitly scoped to the 32 retained boxes and uses 32 as denominator; the claimed domain and the computation domain coincide.", "observed_value": "12/32 = 0.3750 claimed for the 32 retained boxes", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occupancy rate among the 32 retained structurally intact roost boxes: 12/32 = 0.3750 (37.50%)."}]}, {"description": "The report expressly disclaims any extension of the rate to the complete planned set of 40 boxes.", "observed_value": "explicit disclaimer of complete-set claims", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is defined explicitly and only as the\nretained post-screening subset of 32 structurally intact roost boxes. The 8\ndamaged boxes removed at screening are excluded from all rate estimates and\nare reported here solely for complete planned-unit accounting. No claim in\nthis report extends to the complete planned set of 40 boxes."}]}, {"description": "Workflow computes the rate as events among retained divided by number retained, matching the retained-subset claim; recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 8 rows with structurally_intact=no (B03, B07, B12, B18, B21, B29, B33, B40), 32 retained, and 12 retained rows with bats_present=yes.", "observed_value": "n_retained=32, n_events=12, rate=0.3750", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "    retained = [r for r in rows if r[\"structurally_intact\"] == \"yes\"]\n    n_retained = len(retained)\n    n_removed = planned - n_retained"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "B03,no,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest fact potentially supporting the in-scope issue: the report does mention the complete planned set of 40 boxes in its accounting, so a complete-domain reading exists somewhere in the document. However, the 40-box figure appears only as planned-unit accounting and is explicitly excluded from all rate claims, so no rate is attached to the complete domain.", "observed_value": "Planned roost boxes: 40 (accounting only)", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "- Planned roost boxes: 40"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify my no-issue verdict by searching for any statement attaching the 12/32 rate to the complete planned set of 40 boxes, and by recomputing all counts from inputs/data.csv. The recount confirms 40 planned, 8 removed, 32 retained, 12 events, 12/32 = 0.3750, matching the report exactly. The only mention of the 40-unit complete set is in the accounting section and in an explicit disclaimer that no claim extends to it. Additionally, the task itself defines the retained subset as the correct target, so a retained-denominator rate is the mandated deliverable, not a substitution. The falsification attempt failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:d810cbfa19cf81c300ae", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's sole selected result labels 0.3750 (37.50%) as the white-light flare occurrence rate 'for the complete planned set of 40 target stars,' but that value is computed as 12 flaring stars divided by the 32 retained (post-screening) stars. The retained-subset rate is presented as the rate for the complete planned domain of 40 stars, whose actual events-per-planned-unit value from the same data would be 12/40 = 0.3000. This mismatch is confined to the selected result's claimed domain; the accounting counts themselves (40 planned, 32 retained, 8 removed, 12 events) are internally consistent with the input data.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py sets denominator = n_retained (the 32 screened-in stars) while build_report hard-codes the claim language to the complete planned set of `planned` (40) stars; the retained-subset denominator is therefore passed into a complete-domain claim, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation recorded that would authorize the substitution.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "required target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result explicitly claims the rate for the complete planned set of 40 stars while computing it over 32 retained units; 0.3750 = 12/32, whereas 12/40 = 0.3000.", "observed_value": "claimed domain n=40; computation denominator n=32; reported value 0.3750", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] White-light flare occurrence rate for the complete planned set of 40 target stars: 0.3750 (37.50%), computed as 12 flaring stars / 32 exposure units."}]}, {"description": "The scientific-target section reinforces that the reported rate is stated as applying to the complete planned set of 40 stars, so the domain claim is not incidental wording.", "observed_value": "rate stated as applying to all 40 planned stars", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is the complete planned set of 40 M-dwarf\ntarget stars selected for two-minute-cadence photometric monitoring in sector 63.\nThe reported flare occurrence rate is stated as applying to that complete planned\nset of 40 target stars."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source sets the rate denominator to the retained-subset count, not the planned count, before building the complete-domain claim text.", "observed_value": "denominator = n_retained (32), not planned (40)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 74, "end_line": 76, "quoted_text": "    events = sum(1 for u in retained if u[\"flare_detected\"] == \"yes\")\n    denominator = n_retained\n    text = build_report(planned, n_retained, n_removed, events, denominator)"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the screening arithmetic: 8 of 40 stars fail the prespecified rule (coverage < 0.90: TIC-004, TIC-009, TIC-013, TIC-022, TIC-027, TIC-036; saturation_flag = 1: TIC-017, TIC-031, TIC-036), leaving 32 retained, of which 12 have flare_detected = yes; so 0.3750 can only arise from the retained-subset denominator.", "observed_value": "40 planned, 32 retained, 12 events; 12/32 = 0.3750, 12/40 = 0.3000", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "TIC-004,63,0.72,0,NA"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "TIC-017,63,0.96,1,NA"}]}, {"description": "The report itself records that no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists, ruling out an authorized redefinition of the target domain.", "observed_value": "no amendment or approved deviation", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 29, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest counterevidence considered: the selected-result line transparently discloses its computation ('12 flaring stars / 32 exposure units'), and the accounting section separately reports 32 retained and 8 removed, so a careful reader could reconstruct the true retained-subset scope. This mitigates concealment but does not change the fact that the number 0.3750 is asserted as the occurrence rate for the complete planned set of 40 stars, which it is not.", "observed_value": "denominator of 32 disclosed within the claim itself", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "computed as 12 flaring stars / 32 exposure units"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "- Retained after screening: 32\n- Removed by screening: 8"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to defeat the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. (1) Alternative reading: perhaps 'for the complete planned set' merely names the program rather than the rate's domain — but the Scientific target section states the rate 'is stated as applying to that complete planned set of 40 target stars,' which forecloses that reading. (2) Arithmetic: I recomputed from inputs/data.csv; 0.3750 matches only 12/32 (retained subset), while the complete-domain events-per-planned-unit value would be 12/40 = 0.3000, confirming the claimed value belongs to the subset. (3) Authorization: I looked for an amendment or deviation redefining the target to the retained subset; the report explicitly states none exists, and the task mandates the complete planned set. The transparency of the '/ 32 exposure units' disclosure is the only mitigating fact, and it makes the mismatch visible rather than resolving it. The verdict survives falsification.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:fb91e1e5108d106a88d0", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "required target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result claims the rate for the complete planned set of 40 stars and computes it with 40 planned stars as denominator: 12/40 = 0.3000, so the claimed domain and the computation domain match.", "observed_value": "12/40 = 0.3000 claimed for all 40 planned stars", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] White-light flare occurrence rate for the complete planned set of 40 target stars: 0.3000 (30.00%), computed as 12 flaring stars / 40 planned target stars."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source explicitly sets the rate denominator to the full planned count rather than the retained count.", "observed_value": "denominator = planned (40)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 84, "end_line": 86, "quoted_text": "    events = sum(1 for u in retained if u[\"flare_detected\"] == \"yes\")\n    denominator = planned\n    text = build_report(planned, n_retained, n_removed, events, denominator)"}]}, {"description": "The report accurately characterizes the epistemic status of the complete-set rate: the 8 screened-out stars are counted as non-events, the rate is labeled a lower bound on the planned-set flare fraction, and no retained-subset rate is claimed.", "observed_value": "lower-bound framing; removed stars retained in denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "This is a complete-set rate: 12 flare-positive stars per 40 planned target stars.\nFlare status was not assessable for the 8 removed stars, which are therefore\ncounted as non-events, so the reported rate is a lower bound on the flare\nfraction in the planned set. No separate rate is claimed for the 32 retained\nstars."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting: 40 planned rows; 8 fail screening (coverage < 0.90: TIC-004, TIC-009, TIC-013, TIC-022, TIC-027, TIC-036; saturation_flag = 1: TIC-017, TIC-031, TIC-036); 12 retained stars have flare_detected = yes; 12/40 = 0.3000 as reported.", "observed_value": "planned=40, retained=32, removed=8, events=12, rate=0.3000", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "star_id,sector,coverage_fraction,saturation_flag,flare_detected\nTIC-001,63,0.97,0,no"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "- Planned target stars: 40\n- Retained after screening: 32\n- Removed by screening: 8\n- Stars with at least one detected white-light flare (events, among retained): 12"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest fact potentially supporting the in-scope issue: flare detection (the numerator measurement) was performed only on the 32 retained light curves, so the measurement process itself covers only the retained subset. However, the report keeps all 40 planned units in the denominator, counts unassessable stars as non-events, and explicitly labels the result a lower bound for the planned set — so the retained-subset measurement is not substituted for the complete-domain rate; the reported number is genuinely an events-per-planned-unit quantity.", "observed_value": "numerator assessed on retained stars only, with disclosed lower-bound treatment", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "flag is 0. Flare detection was performed only on the retained light curves; the\n8 removed stars remain in the denominator of the selected result."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the issue by checking whether any retained-subset quantity is presented under a complete-domain label. The selected result's value 0.3000 equals 12/40, not the retained-subset value 12/32 = 0.3750, so no subset rate is relabeled; the workflow confirms denominator = planned. I then tested the converse concern — that assessing flares only on retained stars could smuggle a subset-scoped estimate into a complete-set claim — but the report explicitly discloses that removed stars are counted as non-events and bounds the claim as a lower limit, and it claims no separate retained-subset rate. Finally, I recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv and found them consistent with the report. No path to a demonstrated instance of the in-scope issue class succeeded.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}